{
  "problem": {
    "title": "Crude Oil Blending MIP: Maximize Profit with Tier Purchasing",
    "description": "A refinery blends crude oil A and crude oil B to produce two grades of gasoline (I and II). Initial crude A stock is 500 tons; additional crude A can be purchased in three price tiers (up to 500 tons each at 10000, 8000, 6000 yuan/ton, must fill lower tiers before higher ones). Crude B: 1000 tons available at no explicit cost (already owned). Gasoline I requires at least 50% crude A by weight (uAI >= uBI). Gasoline II requires at least 60% crude A by weight (uAII >= 1.5*uBII). Sell prices: gasoline I at 4800 yuan/ton, gasoline II at 5600 yuan/ton. Maximize profit.",
    "problem_type": "mixed_integer_programming",
    "objective": "maximize",
    "objective_description": "Profit = 4800*(uAI+uBI) + 5600*(uAII+uBII) - 10000*buy1 - 8000*buy2 - 6000*buy3",
    "constraints": [
      {
        "description": "Crude A usage: uAI + uAII <= 500 + buy1 + buy2 + buy3"
      },
      {
        "description": "Crude B usage: uBI + uBII <= 1000"
      },
      {
        "description": "Gasoline I blend: uAI >= uBI (at least 50% crude A)"
      },
      {
        "description": "Gasoline II blend: uAII >= 1.5*uBII (at least 60% crude A)"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tier ordering (buy2): buy2 <= 500*z2"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tier fill 1 (buy1 full if buy2>0): buy1 >= 500*z2"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tier ordering (buy3): buy3 <= 500*z3"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tier fill 2 (buy2 full if buy3>0): buy2 >= 500*z3"
      }
    ],
    "decision_variables": [
      "buy1: tons of crude A purchased at tier-1 price (10000 yuan/ton), 0-500",
      "buy2: tons of crude A purchased at tier-2 price (8000 yuan/ton), 0-500",
      "buy3: tons of crude A purchased at tier-3 price (6000 yuan/ton), 0-500",
      "z2: binary, 1 if any tier-2 purchase is made",
      "z3: binary, 1 if any tier-3 purchase is made",
      "uAI: tons of crude A used in gasoline I (continuous, lb=0)",
      "uAII: tons of crude A used in gasoline II (continuous, lb=0)",
      "uBI: tons of crude B used in gasoline I (continuous, lb=0)",
      "uBII: tons of crude B used in gasoline II (continuous, lb=0)"
    ],
    "parameters": [],
    "additional_notes": "Expected obj=5000000. Optimal: buy all 500+500+500=1500 tons A additional + use all 1000 tons B, all for gasoline II: uAII=2000, uBII=1000/1.5... wait, blend_II: uAII >= 1.5*uBII, so uBII <= uAII/1.5. With uAII=1500t-A from purchases + 500t initial = 2000t A available total, uBII <= 2000/1.5=1333. Revenue=5600*(2000+1000)-10000*500-8000*500-6000*500=5600*3000-12000000=16800000-12000000=4800000. Try uAII=1500+500=2000, uBII=1000: check 2000>=1.5*1000=1500 yes. Revenue=5600*3000-24000000=16800000-12000000=4800000. Also try gasoline I: uAI=500, uBI=500: 4800*1000-0=4800000. Let's try maximize: use all 1000t B in gasoline II (5600>4800). uBII=1000, need uAII>=1500. uAII=1500, buy1=500,buy2=500,buy3=0: cost=10000*500+8000*500=9000000, revenue=5600*2500=14000000, profit=5000000. Yes obj=5000000! All-scalar no CSV. Objective constructed left-to-right: subtract(subtract(subtract(sum(multiply(4800,sum(uAI,uBI)),multiply(5600,sum(uAII,uBII))),multiply(10000,buy1)),multiply(8000,buy2)),multiply(6000,buy3)).",
    "csv_file_paths": {}
  },
